# Centred controls and contextual help

Centre the Board edit-mode selector, present the Cards/Constructions choice in the middle of the screen, and add circular question-mark help controls to the relevant editing and plan screens.

## Acceptance criteria

- [x] Terrain/Numbers remains horizontally centred independently of the trailing help button.
- [x] Choosing New Plan presents Cards/Constructions in a modal box centred on screen.
- [x] The plan-type box contains a circular question-mark help button and Cancel action.
- [x] Cards and Constructions are stacked vertically, with Cards above Constructions.
- [x] Board editing, plan editing, and Plan Browser each expose a circular question-mark help button.
- [x] Plan Browser graph and help controls use independent tap targets and cannot activate one another.
- [x] The construction-plan preview control sits immediately to the right of the top player selector.
- [x] Every help button presents concise contextual guidance rather than being decorative.
- [x] Existing player-selector ordering and stable Board positioning are preserved.
- [ ] Focused UI checks pass on a functioning simulator.

## Implementation notes

- Board uses a `ZStack` so the segmented control stays centred while help remains trailing.
- The plan-type chooser is an in-view material modal with a dimmed backdrop and scale/opacity transition.
- Plan Browser consolidates help and default-plan messages in one typed alert state.

## Evidence

- UI coverage checks the Terrain/Numbers midpoint, centred plan-type chooser, and all requested help controls.
- UI coverage checks that graph/help taps remain independent, plan types are vertically ordered, and the construction preview sits to the right of the player selector.
- `xcodebuild build-for-testing -quiet -project Catanalyst.xcodeproj -scheme Catanalyst -destination 'generic/platform=iOS Simulator' -derivedDataPath /private/tmp/Catanalyst-help-layout-derived` succeeded for the app and both test bundles.
- The revised app and test bundles compile using `/private/tmp/Catanalyst-layout-corrections-derived`.

## Remaining risks and manual checks

- Run the focused UI scenarios after CoreSimulator is stable.
- Manually review modal centring, help copy, Dynamic Type wrapping, and compact-screen spacing.
